                <pb facs="0503" n="497" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg497"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851R.00/136: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom (Matthews) to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-30T19:00:00+01:00">December 30,
                            1942—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7441. Department’s 6631, December 29, 4 p.m. Kuh was given this story by French
                    contacts at Carlton Gardens. With the possible exception of point 4 it
                    represents closely the views of all the Fighting French. None of them to whom I
                    have talked personally or whose conversations have been reported to me has shown
                    any conception of an agreement with General Giraud and North African elements on
                    any basis other than de Gaulle and National Committee political supremacy. As I
                    have reported (please see my telegram 7407, December 29, 6 p.m.<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d497-f1"/>) they consider that de Gaulle is the one man to whom the
                    French people have entrusted their hope for a better future. Furthermore their
                    jobs are at stake. I see no indication that our British friends are endeavoring
                    to discourage the high and unrealistic hopes of the National Committee and de
                    Gaulle’s immediate entourage.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Murphy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Matthews</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
